# IRL moderation service environment (production). Copy to /etc/irl/moderation.env ON THE SERVER, mode 600, owner root.
# NEVER commit the filled file. Nothing here is a real secret.

# At least 16 characters; THE SAME VALUE as MODERATION_SERVICE_KEY in backend.env. The service refuses to start without it
# and refuses every request that does not carry it. Generate ON THE SERVER (once) and paste into BOTH files:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
MODERATION_SERVICE_KEY=

# The optional AI understanding of Explore requests (Phase 17G-3) stays OFF: set none of the IRL_UNDERSTANDING_* variables
# (see moderation-service/kurinji_moderation/understand.py) unless you decide to use a provider; its key would live ONLY here,
# and EXPLORE_UNDERSTANDING_MODE=ON would then be set in backend.env. Typed Explore words are sent to that provider if you do.
